# Every branch prepends to the top of CHANGELOG.md, so two branches in flight
# always conflict on the same first lines; union keeps both sides' added lines.
# Deliberate — see the repository map in AGENTS.md before changing it.
#
# The pattern has no slash, so git matches it at ANY depth, not just here. That
# is left as it is on purpose, and the reasoning is worth keeping because the
# shape invites a "fix". After fusion the obvious worry was that codex's and
# ox's own changelogs would land at stacks/<name>/CHANGELOG.md and inherit
# union-merge without anyone deciding it. They did not: neither stack brought a
# changelog, and this repository has exactly one, at the root. So the widening
# is real in mechanism and empty in practice — `git check-attr` already answers
# `merge: union` for stacks/codex/CHANGELOG.md and stacks/ox-alpha/CHANGELOG.md,
# paths that do not exist.
#
# Anchoring this to /CHANGELOG.md would therefore change no behaviour today,
# which is exactly why it is not worth doing: it would trade a rule that keeps
# working when a sibling changelog appears for one that quietly stops. The
# consequence to know is the other direction — a sibling changelog added later
# inherits union-merge silently, with no decision made at the time. Union is
# safe only for a file shaped like this one: one bullet per entry on its own
# line, and repeating ### Added / ### Changed / ### Fixed headings, so a
# duplicated heading is the file's normal shape rather than damage. A new
# changelog that is not shaped that way needs this line anchored, and this
# comment is the record that the choice was made once and left open.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
